hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22258","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfa, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, from Sufyan ibn Abi Zuhayr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever keeps a dog that does not benefit him for crops or udders, a qirat decreases from his work every day. Al-Saib said: So I said to Sufyan: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Yes, by the Lord of this mosque."
"22259","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, informed us, Yazid ibn Khusayfa informed me that Busr ibn Said informed him that he heard in the gathering of the Laythis mentioning that Sufyan informed them that his horse tired at al-Aqiq while he was in a detachment the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had sent them in, so he returned to him seeking a mount. Sufyan claimed, as they mentioned, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out with him seeking a camel for him, and he found none except with Abu Jahm ibn Hudhayfa al-Adawi, so he bargained for him. Abu Jahm said to him: I will not sell it to you, O Messenger of Allah, but take it and mount upon it whomever you wish. He claimed that he took it from him, then went out until when he reached Bir al-Ihab, he claimed that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Buildings are about to reach this place, and Sham is about to be opened, and men from the people of this land will come to it, and its countryside and ease will please them, while Madina is better for them had they known. Then Iraq will be opened, and a people will come urging, carrying their families and whoever obeys them, while Madina is better for them had they known. Ibrahim prayed for the people of Makka, and I ask Allah, Blessed and Exalted, to bless for us in our sa and to bless for us in our mudd like what He blessed for the people of Makka."
"22260","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Hisham ibn Urwa informed me, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Sufyan ibn Abi Zuhayr al-Bahzi, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Yemen will be opened, and a people will come urging, carrying their families and whoever obeys them, while Madina is better for them had they known."
"22261","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Malik informed me, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Sufyan ibn Abi Zuhayr, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Yemen will be opened, and a people will come urging, and he mentioned the hadith."
"22262","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Sufyan ibn Abi Zuhayr, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr said: I was informed that he was at the Mawsim, so I came to him and asked him, and he informed me. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: You will open Sham, and peoples will come urging. He said: All of them were opened. And he said: Urging."
"22263","Rawh narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfa, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, that he informed him that he heard Sufyan ibn Abi Zuhayr, and he is a man from Shanu'a from the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrating to people with him at the door of the mosque, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever keeps a dog that does not benefit him for crops nor udders, a qirat decreases from his work every day. He said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Yes, by the Lord of this mosque."
